WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.384 --> 00:00:04.958
- [Host] Budapest, Hungary,
one of Europe's hidden jewels.

00:00:04.958 --> 00:00:06.813
A tourist hotspot known for its history

00:00:06.813 --> 00:00:11.539
and beautiful architecture
and its love of water.

00:00:11.539 --> 00:00:13.848
But while most splash above the surface,

00:00:13.848 --> 00:00:16.928
below the city is a
secret subterranean world.

00:00:16.928 --> 00:00:19.845
(mysterious music)

00:00:23.902 --> 00:00:27.345
Hungary's capital is home to
over 80 geothermal springs

00:00:27.345 --> 00:00:28.923
and dozens of baths,

00:00:28.923 --> 00:00:32.677
all heated by the earth's
warmth deep below the surface.

00:00:32.677 --> 00:00:35.806
As this naturally heated
water flowed beneath the city,

00:00:35.806 --> 00:00:37.790
it carved out hundreds of caves,

00:00:37.790 --> 00:00:40.303
making the city home to
the largest collection

00:00:40.303 --> 00:00:42.803
of thermal caves in the world.

00:00:47.522 --> 00:00:50.888
The crown jewel of this system
is the Molnár János cave.

00:00:50.888 --> 00:00:54.191
Discovered in the 19th
century by János Molnár,

00:00:54.191 --> 00:00:57.370
who traced the warm spring
waters from the lake outside

00:00:57.370 --> 00:00:59.953
to its source beneath the city.

00:01:05.318 --> 00:01:08.728
Divers first started to
explore the cave in the 1950s.

00:01:08.728 --> 00:01:11.892
Since then, nearly four miles
of tunnels have been charted.

00:01:11.892 --> 00:01:14.475
(gentle music)

00:01:20.852 --> 00:01:22.502
In the pitch black of the cave,

00:01:22.502 --> 00:01:24.457
miles of rope have been laid for divers

00:01:24.457 --> 00:01:28.207
to follow the correct
route back to the exit.

00:01:29.492 --> 00:01:31.002
The water is naturally warm,

00:01:31.002 --> 00:01:34.085
between 70 and 80 degrees fahrenheit.

00:01:35.299 --> 00:01:38.512
The rooms of the cave can
range from tiny to massive.

00:01:38.512 --> 00:01:40.127
The largest is so large,

00:01:40.127 --> 00:01:43.127
it can hold 350 double decker buses.

00:01:45.025 --> 00:01:48.451
And even in the pitch
black, life has found a way.

00:01:48.451 --> 00:01:50.712
Biologists have identified new species

00:01:50.712 --> 00:01:53.212
that live only in these caves.

00:01:55.036 --> 00:01:57.549
Much is still to be
answered about this place,

00:01:57.549 --> 00:02:00.349
a reminder that even in
the most urban of areas,

00:02:00.349 --> 00:02:04.516
you can still find some of
nature's greatest wonders.

